\ ******************************************************************
\ *	loader.6502 - OSFILE a packed stream into a staging area, unpack it out
\ ******************************************************************
\ *	beeb-port-kit, MIT, Kieran Connell 2026. Baron syntax, plain 6502.
\ *
\ *	WHAT IT IS. Edge's boot loader, generalised: every data file on the
\ *	disc ships compressed with a catalogue load address the disc
\ *	builder writes (py/make_disc.py), and none of them could be loaded
\ *	straight to where it belongs even uncompressed - the filing system
\ *	has the DFS ROM paged in at &8000 while it works, so a bank's bytes
\ *	would land in the ROM socket, and on a Master HAZEL is the filing
\ *	system's own workspace. So each stages in RAM and is unpacked from
\ *	there. ALL OF IT RUNS BEFORE install_irq (irq.6502) - not because
\ *	the DFS needs the MOS's interrupt (measured 2026-09-09: it loads
\ *	with IRQ1V taken, and with interrupts masked outright), but because
\ *	a load costs whole frames.
\ *
\ *	WHERE IT CAME FROM.
\ *	  https://github.com/kieranhj/edge-beeb/blob/master/src/main.asm
\ *	    (load_stream / unpack_to / load_bank / unpack_andy / load_hazel,
\ *	    ~1712-1840)
\ *	  https://github.com/kieranhj/edge-beeb/blob/master/src/tables.asm
\ *	    (the OSFILE parameter block, ~33-47)
\ *	  https://github.com/kieranhj/edge-beeb/blob/master/lib/disksys.asm
\ *	    (the same block; Edge's boot uses OSFILE, not disksys)
\ *	Paradroid loads by `*LOAD` through OSCLI instead (its ts_loads,
\ *	main.asm ~2570-2600, and UnpackBankIn) - the same staging idea with
\ *	a command string per file. It is NOT ported here: OSFILE takes a
\ *	filename pointer and a block, which is the smaller thing to
\ *	generalise, and Edge's is the later of the two.
\ *
\ *	WHAT WAS MEASURED, and when:
\ *	  - OSFILE WRITES THE FILE'S CATALOGUE ADDRESSES BACK INTO ITS
\ *	    PARAMETER BLOCK after a load, so the next call would honour the
\ *	    LAST file's load address and land wherever that was. load_stream
\ *	    resets load and exec before every call (Edge, 2026-09-03; it
\ *	    was the second bank landing on the first).
\ *	  - Sideways RAM is written through ROMSEL alone; a Solidisk-style
\ *	    board needing its write-enable latches is refused, not driven
\ *	    (Paradroid swram_probe.6502, KC 2026-08-29).
\ *	  - Writing &F4 as well as &FE30 before the load matters: the DFS
\ *	    pages its ROM in over the bank and the MOS restores ROMSEL from
\ *	    &F4 afterwards, so the unpack lands in the bank named there.
\ *	  - MASTER ONLY. ANDY is 4K at &8000-&8FFF, ROMSEL bit 7, overlaying
\ *	    only that 4K of whichever bank is paged (Edge, jsbeeb
\ *	    2026-09-04, from 6502 in main RAM: &AA to &8000 under bank 4 and
\ *	    &55 under &84 read back separately; &9000 is the bank either
\ *	    way). The test HAS to be machine code: BASIC is itself the ROM
\ *	    at &8000. The loader cannot write into ANDY while the filing
\ *	    system runs, so its stream is loaded early and unpacked last.
\ *	    THE MOS WRITES THREE OF ITS PAGES (1942 port, jsbeeb Master
\ *	    2026-09-11): &80 on *KEY, &8800-&882F on EVERY MODE CHANGE AND
\ *	    SOFT BREAK, &8F on VDU 23. Loads, *CAT and the sound leave it
\ *	    alone. So all 4K is yours only if the unpack follows the last
\ *	    mode change and nothing issues *KEY or VDU 23 afterwards; else
\ *	    use &8100-&87FF and &8900-&8EFF. docs/hardware-facts.md, ANDY,
\ *	    has the page map.
\ *	  - MASTER ONLY. HAZEL (&C000-&DFFF, ACCCON bit 3) is the filing
\ *	    system's workspace, but not all of it is in use. load_hazel
\ *	    unpacks into HAZEL_FREE-HAZEL_TOP (&C300-&DEFF, 7K), which
\ *	    OSFILE loads, saves and deletes never write, so the disc stays
\ *	    usable after it (jsbeeb Master, MOS 3.20, 1770 DFS,
\ *	    2026-09-11). What does write into the window afterwards: any *
\ *	    command (&DC), an open file (&C3, and a page each from &C4), a
\ *	    soft BREAK (&C3 and &DA) - which does find the DFS again. Not
\ *	    measured: MOS 3.5, MMFS, real hardware. docs/hardware-facts.md,
\ *	    HAZEL, has the map.
\ *	    Edge unpacked over all 8K from &C000 instead, DFS's own pages
\ *	    included. A load like that must be the last disc access, and
\ *	    BREAK must then be a power-on reset, because a soft break leaves
\ *	    the wreckage in place - measured: no DFS banner, *CAT returns
\ *	    nothing. OSBYTE 200, X = 3 at the top of main makes BREAK a
\ *	    power-on reset (bit 1) and disables ESCAPE (bit 0):
\ *	        lda #200 : ldx #3 : ldy #0 : jsr osbyte
\ *	    Do it FIRST, before anything can be broken into.
\ *
\ *	THE INCLUDER DEFINES, before this file is included:
\ *	  zxsrc, zxdst (ZP)   the depacker's pointers (zx02depack.6502)
\ *	  zx_unpack           the depacker's entry, whichever depacker that
\ *	                      is: zx02depack.6502 for a new port, zx0depack.6502
\ *	                      for a ZX0 disc. It was called zx0_unpack before
\ *	                      2026-09-07 and still is in the two shipping ports.
\ *	  LOADER_STAGE        the page-aligned address streams stage at for
\ *	                      load_bank / load_hazel. Edge: DEPK_STREAM =
\ *	                      &3000, the SHADOW screen, 20K nobody displays
\ *	                      while the loading picture is up in main.
\ *	                      Paradroid: DEPK_STREAM = &3200 in the
\ *	                      framebuffer, blanked. It must not overlap the
\ *	                      output (the in-place rule, zx02depack.6502).
\ *	  MASTER              0 or 1: assembles load_hazel and unpack_andy.
\ *	The filenames are the includer's: CR-terminated strings, the
\ *	address in A/Y.
\ *
\ *	Fork this into your project; keep this header.
\ ******************************************************************

\ ---- load_stream: A/Y = filename, X = the page it loads at ---------
\ Leaves zxsrc pointing at it, ready for unpack_to. Clobbers A, X, Y.
.load_stream
{
    stx stream_page
    sta osfile_nameaddr
    sty osfile_nameaddr+1

    \\ OSFILE writes the file's catalogue addresses back into the block
    \\ after a load, so the next call would honour the last file's load
    \\ address and land wherever that was. Reset load and exec every call
    \\ (exec low byte 0 = "use the block's load address").
    \\ THE LOAD ADDRESS IS &FFFFxxxx, THE HOST'S. With a second processor
    \\ attached, &0000xxxx means the PARASITE: the DFS sends the file over
    \\ the Tube and the host hangs in the Tube code (measured, jsbeeb B +
    \\ 65C02 and Master + 65C102, 2026-09-11: PC in &0400-&07FF, the game
    \\ never past its first load). Without a Tube the top bytes are ignored.
    lda #&ff
    sta osfile_loadaddr+2
    sta osfile_loadaddr+3
    lda #0
    sta osfile_loadaddr
    sta osfile_execaddr
    lda stream_page
    sta osfile_loadaddr+1

    ldx #LO(osfile_params)
    ldy #HI(osfile_params)
    lda #&FF                    ; OSFILE &FF: load, to the block's address
    jsr osfile

    \\ AFTER the call, not before: the depacker's zero page is borrowed
    \\ from the game's, and the filing system may be running in it.
    lda #0
    sta zxsrc
    lda stream_page
    sta zxsrc+1
    rts
    .stream_page EQUB 0
}

\ ---- unpack_to: the stream at zxsrc to X:A ------------------------
.unpack_to
{
    sta zxdst
    stx zxdst+1
    jmp zx_unpack
}

\ ---- load_bank: A/Y = filename, X = the ROMSEL value of the bank ---
\ Stages the stream at LOADER_STAGE and unpacks it straight into the
\ paged-in bank at &8000. Leaves the bank selected.
.load_bank
{
    stx ROMSHAD                 ; both: the DFS pages its ROM in over
    stx ROMSEL                  ; us and the MOS restores from ROMSHAD
    ldx #HI(LOADER_STAGE)
    jsr load_stream
    lda #LO(SWRAM_BASE)
    ldx #HI(SWRAM_BASE)
    jmp unpack_to
}

IF MASTER
\ ---- unpack_andy: the stream at zxsrc into ANDY at X:A -------------
\ Called AFTER the last load, with zxsrc already pointing at a stream
\ loaded earlier (the loader cannot write into ANDY while the filing
\ system runs). With interrupts off and ROMSHAD set as well as ROMSEL:
\ the MOS's IRQ handler is still installed here, and anything that
\ pages a ROM restores ROMSEL from ROMSHAD - which would drop ANDY out
\ from under the depacker half way through and put the rest of the
\ stream into the bank underneath. Puts the bank back on the way out
\ (Edge does not: its caller's next instruction does).
.unpack_andy
{
    \\ THE DESTINATION SURVIVES THE PAGING. This used to page ANDY in
    \\ through A and then `jsr unpack_to`, which reads A:X as the
    \\ destination - by when A held ROMSHAD OR &80, so a stream for &8100
    \\ landed at &8187. Nothing had called it until the 1942 port's in-play
    \\ text (its BUGS.md #21), whose code then ran 135 bytes out.
    \\ 1942 stores zxdst here and jumps to zx_unpack; this parks the low
    \\ byte in Y instead, because a port that assembles unpack_andy but
    \\ never calls it (the template's MASTER build) would otherwise get
    \\ Baron's "ZA_AUTO used in code unreachable" warning on every build.
    \\ lib/test/andy_test.6502 runs it.
    tay
    sei
    lda ROMSHAD
    pha
    ora #ANDY_ROMSEL
    sta ROMSHAD
    sta ROMSEL
    tya
    jsr unpack_to
    pla
    sta ROMSHAD
    sta ROMSEL
    cli
    rts
}

\ ---- load_hazel: A/Y = filename, unpacked into HAZEL at &C300 ------
\ Stages at LOADER_STAGE and unpacks with ACCCON's Y bit set over the
\ unpack, into the window the DFS leaves alone (HAZEL_FREE, &C300 up to
\ HAZEL_TOP, &DF00). OSFILE loads may follow it; * commands and open
\ files write into the window - see the header. The unpacked stream
\ must end by HAZEL_TOP: nothing checks it at run time.
.load_hazel
{
    ldx #HI(LOADER_STAGE)
    jsr load_stream
    lda ACCCON
    ora #ACCCON_Y
    sta ACCCON
    lda #LO(HAZEL_FREE)
    ldx #HI(HAZEL_FREE)
    jsr unpack_to
    lda ACCCON
    and #255-ACCCON_Y
    sta ACCCON
    rts
}
ENDIF

\ ---- claim_nmi: take the NMI once the last load is done ------------
\ OSBYTE 143 with X = 12 asks the paged ROMs to hand over the NMI, which
\ the filing system gives up (its routine lives at NMI_CODE, &0D00); an
\ RTI goes there so a stray NMI returns. Unlike *TAPE (OSBYTE 140) it
\ does not unplug the filing system: it claims the NMI back if anything
\ loads again, and nothing forces a *DISC afterwards on someone who
\ booted from MMFS or ADFS. Only Econet is likely to mind. hexwab's
\ method (paradroid-beeb issue #18); Paradroid, jsbeeb 2026-09-10:
\ &0D00 reads &40 at the title and the game plays. Call it AFTER the
\ last disc access. Clobbers A, X, Y.
NMI_CODE = &0D00
.claim_nmi
{
    lda #143
    ldx #12
    ldy #&ff
    jsr osbyte
    lda #&40                    ; RTI
    sta NMI_CODE
    rts
}

\ ---- the OSFILE parameter block -----------------------------------
\ Boot-only data in both ports: read while the disc is loading and never
\ again. Edge keeps it above SPR_SAVE's base with the rest of the boot
\ code, where the game walks over it once it starts.
.osfile_params
.osfile_nameaddr
EQUW 0                          ; -> the CR-terminated filename
.osfile_loadaddr
EQUD 0                          ; rewritten by every load - see the header
.osfile_execaddr
EQUD 0                          ; low byte 0 = use loadaddr
.osfile_length
EQUD 0                          ; OSFILE fills these two in on the way
.osfile_endaddr
EQUD 0                          ; back; nothing here reads them
